  "source_anchor": "arXiv:2609.06905v1, Section 2.2, equations (2.6)-(2.7): Gaussian-noise density dependency",
  "target_statement": "For every finite-dimensional real inner-product Borel space E and eta>0, the map of stdGaussian E by z -> sqrt(eta) z is volume.withDensity of ofReal((sqrt(2*pi*eta))^(-finrank R E) * exp(-norm(z)^2/(2*eta))). The natural-power inverse normalizer includes dimension zero. This is only the isotropic-noise density dependency; the augmentation identity is a separate next edge.",
